{"id":"tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-8233516149842295530.post-4419425358435558760","year":"2020","month":"09","slug":"read-vs-sql-select-quick-performance","path":"/2020/09/read-vs-sql-select-quick-performance.html","title":"READ vs SQL SELECT, A Quick Performance Test - Part 2","published":"2020-09-24T11:11:00Z","updated":"2025-01-13T07:52:34.161Z","labels":["RPGLE","IBM i","SQL"],"excerpt":"We have seen the comparison between READ and SQL SELECT (with CURSOR & Fetch one record at a time) and SQL SELECT has run about 30% less time than READ (70% of READ). Click Here to see more...","readingMinutes":2,"youtubeId":null,"youtubeThumb":false,"coverImage":null,"headings":[],"html":"<p>We have seen the comparison between READ and SQL SELECT (with CURSOR &amp; Fetch one record at a time) and SQL SELECT has run about 30% less time than READ (70% of READ). <a href=\"/2020/09/read-vs-sql-select-quick-performance_23.html\">Click Here</a> to see more details on this.</p><p>However, Fetching more number of Records into a Multi Occurrence Data Structure and looping the data through DS should run even faster. We would be using same Table created in Part - 1, Please see Part - 1 using the above link for these details.</p><p>We will see a sample program with FETCH multiple rows into DS and compare the results. </p><p>Program with SELECT (PPSQL1):</p><div><pre data-role=\"code\" data-lang=\"rpgle\"><code><span style=\"color:#6A737D\">**Free</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dcl-S</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wSql </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">50</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dcl-Ds</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wResult </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Qualified</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">DIM</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">9999</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">  wCol1 </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">10</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">  wCol2 </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">10</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">  wCol3 </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">10</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">  wCol4 </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">10</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">END-DS</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dcl-S</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wCol1 </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">10</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dcl-S</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wCol2 </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">10</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dcl-S</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wCol3 </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">10</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dcl-S</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wCol4 </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">10</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dcl-S</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wCount </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Packed</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">7</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">:</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Inz</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dcl-S</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wTotalRecords </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Packed</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">4</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">:</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Inz</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dcl-S</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wCurrentRecord </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Packed</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">4</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">:</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Inz</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dcl-S</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wStartTime </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">8</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dcl-S</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wEndTime </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">8</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dcl-S</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wText </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">50</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">wStartTime </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">%Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">%Time</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">()) ;</span></code></pre></div><div><pre data-role=\"code\" data-lang=\"rpgle\"><code><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">wSql </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">'Select * From PTESTTABL Order By TCOLUMN1'</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Exec Sql</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> Prepare wQuery from </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">:</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">wSql ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Exec Sql</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> Declare C1 Cursor </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">for</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wQuery ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Exec Sql</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Open</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> C1 ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Exec Sql</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> Fetch Next From C1 </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">For</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">9999</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> rows Into </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">:</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">wResult ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dow</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> SqlErrd(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">3</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">  wTotalRecords </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> SqlErrd(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">3</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">  wCurrentRecord </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">  </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dow</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wCurrentRecord </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wTotalRecords ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">    wCount </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">+=</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">    wCurrentRecord </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">+=</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">  </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">EndDo</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">  </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">If</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> SqlErrd(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">5</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">) </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">100</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">    </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Leave</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">  </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">EndIf</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">  </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Exec Sql</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> Fetch Next From C1 </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">For</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">9999</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> rows Into </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">:</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">wResult ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">EndDo</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Exec Sql</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">Close</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> C1 ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">wEndTime </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">%Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">%Time</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">()) ;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">wText </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">'Start: '</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">+</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wStartTime</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">      </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">+</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">' End: '</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">+</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wEndTime</span>\n<span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">      </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">+</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">' Records: '</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">+</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">%Char</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(wCount) ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#F97583\">Dsply</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> wText ;</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">*InLr</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> </span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\">*On</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> ;</span></code></pre></div><p>Now, This program took just 2 seconds to read one million records, which is much faster than using READ (&gt; 70% Faster) and SELECT with single record for every FETCH (&gt; 60% Faster).</p><div><div><pre data-role=\"output\" data-lang=\"text\"><code>CALL PPSQL1\nDSPLY  Start: 10.40.52 End: 10.40.54 Records: 1000000</code></pre></div><p>Please note that,  File Size and Data are same as used in the Part - 1.</p> </div>"}